# Written by `next dev` into the application it is serving, on every start.
#
# The same rule as apps/driver-portal/.gitignore, and the reasoning is there: these are the
# generator's files rather than this repository's, they are untracked and unignored so `git add -A`
# collects them, and the rule is app-local because the root .gitignore is a shared surface and this
# file is not. `git add -f` if this application ever wants instructions of its own.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
